Only Run: Sigma-1 - (mu-1)/2 = R/2 - 1/2  -> with R = 1+eps: epsilon/2
Only Run: mu*eta = 2 Sigma - mu = R  (GRUT family: mu*eta = 1)
Horndeski small-alpha ratio limits: f(R) r=-1 -> 0 (Sigma=1);  alpha_M->0 (r->oo) -> 1 (no slip, Sigma=mu);  alpha_B=0 (r=0) -> 1/2 (GRUT line)
GRUT family: Sigma = alpha*x/2 + 1 ; ratio (Sigma-1)/(mu-1) = 1/2 for all x, alpha
Staying on the line at all a in Only Run needs eps(a) = 0 for all a => M_* constant => alpha_M = dln M_*^2/dln a = 0 => GR
